# Product / UX standing preferences

- Use open source (or a reputable free tier of an OSS product) before building commodity systems: analytics, charts, email, CMS, search, observability.
- Custom code is for FindMyInvite-specific invitation experience, not Mixpanel clones.
- Keep `/akay` unlinked from public pages if it remains.
- Do not store analytics events in the guest invitations database.
- Hosts sign in with email and password to save a draft or publish. Forgot password is backlog; do not build it until Ashok asks.
- Operator Shortlist, Competitors, and Upcoming cards lead with a page preview of the existing http(s) link. Do not make those desks text-only.
- Gallery collection tabs are Premium, Elite, Free (not Royal/Classics). Premium: Sita Kalyanam, Velicha Poove, Rosu Rosu Rosu, Gold Dream, Ponmaalai. Elite: remaining Royal designs. Free: all Classics. Retired assembly iterations stay off the gallery. The newest Premium clone is always the default Assembly parent.
- `/assembly` is a one-viewport mobile wizard: Pinterest URL → song → first/last opening stills → **Proceed to generate (Rs. 499)** → demo preview. No page scroll; next step by transition. Stills are free; video + site start only after that button. No payment gateway until Ashok asks. FIRST still prefix: 10ft solid-gold arched double door, marble arch, lawn, layered lanterns, no humans; then pin-true handle/charms and the door fills the 9:16 frame. Opening video: 8k cinematic 2.5D parallax wrap; after the doors open, bullet-time ultra slowmo on levitating bold white 3D handwritten SAVE THE DATE; then glide to the couple. Opening is xAI first+last only — do not fall back to Replicate without Ashok's permission; show an alert on xAI credit/API failure.
- Premium cinematic clones: v1.5 assembled on the laptop (Approach B). **v1.6** runs `/assembly` on findmyinvite.com in a Vercel Pro Sandbox, pushes GitHub branch `assembly/{id}`, Vercel preview-deploys. Ashok says **Publish** → Akay merges to `main` (ask twice) and applies Supabase `template_catalog` SQL. Playbook: `documents/assembly-publish.md`. Ashok does not run SQL. Assembly UI shows preview + GitHub links only (no file/migration dumps). Display names are editable before assemble. GitHub branches/forks are how we customize a template later — do not flatten clones onto Blob-only rows.
- `/assembly/pipeline` is the operator kanban: live columns for cloud jobs, asset links, prompt downloads, Resume push, and **Approve to live catalogue** (queues Publish for Akay — never auto-merges `main`). Wizard stays the phone create flow; pipeline is the ops desk.
